WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.660
[upbeat music]

2
00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:06.900
In past courses, you learned a bit
about packaging chiplets into a system.

3
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.200
But did you know
that integrating multiple chips,

4
00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:14.580
often from different process technologies,
has been practiced for decades?

5
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:18.840
Standard wire bond and flip
chip on substrate technologies,

6
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:23.130
known as 2D packaging, are commonly
employed to combine disparate

7
00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:28.420
technologies in a single package for
performance or form factor considerations.

8
00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:33.700
The cost incurred in these cases
is minimal, and in some instances,

9
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.040
it may even be lower than the cost
of individually packaging each die.

10
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:44.060
Multi-chip packaging serves multiple
purposes, minimizing interface losses,

11
00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:48.000
separating different technologies
such as logic and analog,

12
00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:51.500
and increasing product value
through added functionality.

13
00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:56.240
The reasons for multi-chip
packaging also applies to chiplets.

14
00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:01.520
Remember, chiplets are a product
strategy enabled by packaging.

15
00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:06.020
By creating a portfolio of reusable
and interchangeable blocks,

16
00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:11.720
chiplets allow products to be brought
to market faster with lower R&D costs.

17
00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:16.420
The choice of packaging impacts
factors like power efficiency,

18
00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:20.600
interconnect density,
and manufacturing complexity.

19
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:24.720
Chiplet packaging also
unlocks new opportunities,

20
00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:29.780
such as optimizing silicon technology
nodes for specific functionalities,

21
00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:34.400
bridging products for socket
security before product optimization,

22
00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:38.320
and enabling higher value
systems with increased margin.

23
00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:44.490
A chiplet product packaging platform must
meet performance and cost requirements

24
00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:48.800
while offering scalability across
product tiers and generations.

25
00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.880
Now that we've explored
the fundamentals of chiplet packaging,

26
00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:58.680
let's examine a key aspect of packaging,
chip-to-chip interface requirements.

27
00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:01.250
High performance chiplet integration

28
00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:03.940
depends on advanced
interconnect technologies.

29
00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:05.460
Let's dive in.

30
00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:10.780
[upbeat music]

